ectal endosonography in benign anorectal disease, emphasizing its ease of performance, short learning curve, and high accuracy in visualizing the anal sphincters and pelvic floor structures. Therefore, anorectal endosonography is valuable in diagnosing dyschesia.\",\n\"answer_choice\": \"A\"\n}", "prompt_tokens": 5647, "output_tokens": 265, "llm": {"prefill_s": 2.710401, "decode_s": 4.675388}, "choice": "A", "correct": true}
